course: dictionary
lesson: 15875
title: Unification: joining into one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unification is a long word, but it is built from parts you may know. Unify means to make into one, and the ending -tion shows an act or event. So unification is the act of joining separate things into one whole. «The unification of the two small villages made one larger town.» The villages were separate, and now they are one.
explain: Unification can describe groups or countries too. «German unification happened in 1871, when many separate states joined to form one country.» The word names the event of joining, not the thing that is joined. In history lessons you will meet phrases such as the unification of Italy.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. Words like separate, joined, one or whole show that unification is about bringing parts together. If a sentence talks about splitting or breaking apart, the meaning is the opposite. To check, put your meaning into the sentence: does «the act of joining separate things into one» still make sense?
fact: Unification means the act of joining separate things, groups or countries into one whole.
fact: «The unification of the schools» means the schools were joined together into one.
fact: «German unification» means the joining of many German states, which happened in 1871.
fact: Unification is a noun: it names an act or event.
fact: The word comes from unify, which means to make into one.
exercise: «The two small clubs chose to merge, and the unification made one strong team.» What does unification mean here? | Splitting one thing into many pieces | *Joining separate things into one | Painting a picture of a team | Losing a match
exercise: What does German unification name? | A school trip to Germany | The shrinking of a country's borders | A German meal eaten by many people | *The joining of many German states in 1871
exercise: Which word in this sentence names the act of joining? «The unification of the towns made one city.» | towns | *unification | made | city
test: «The unification of Italy happened in the 1800s, joining many separate states.» What does the unification of Italy describe? | A holiday in Rome | *The joining of separate states into one country | A new kind of pasta | A map of Italy
test: Which word is the opposite of unification? | Union | *Division | Unity | Joining
exam: «After the unification, the two villages shared one school, one shop and one name.» What happened to the villages? | They split into three small villages | *They joined and became one place | They forgot their names | They moved to a new country by boat
